# BLASTI Mobile — production build environment (applied to the WEB bundle that
# gets exported into the APK when BLASTI_MOBILE_BUILD=1 — see
# apps/web/next.config.ts readMobileReleaseEnv()).
#
# ─── WHY THIS FILE IS COMMITTED (update-in-place + "can not load" fixes) ─────
# CI-built APKs used to ship with NO baked server URL and full LAN discovery:
#   • fresh installs depended on a LAN scan that only succeeds when a desktop
#     BLASTI server happens to run on the same Wi-Fi — otherwise every API
#     call died against the useless http://10.0.2.2:3003 emulator fallback
#     ("can not load this page" / blank data);
#   • a manual FULL SYNC wipes localStorage (last-known-good URL included),
#     so afterwards the app could not re-find the server at all.
# With NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_DISCOVERY=0 the resolver is PRODUCTION-LOCKED: it
# resolves synchronously to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — no scans, no 10.0.2.2
# fallback, deterministic boot on every install and after every full sync.
#
# NOTE: locked builds do NOT offer the LAN-desktop discovery UI. That is the
# intended trade-off for phone builds whose sync/update/push flows all target
# the VPS. Point the URL at a new server by editing this one line.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://129.151.242.219
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_DISCOVERY=0
